# TOML File Rules

When working with TOML configuration files:

## Best Practices
- Use consistent indentation (2 spaces preferred)
- Group related settings together with `[section]` headers
- Add comments above complex configuration options
- Keep lists sorted alphabetically when it makes sense
- Use double quotes for string values that may contain special characters

## Common Patterns
```toml
[section]
enabled = true
directory = "path/to/dir"

[section.subsection]
max_items = 10
```

**This rule should be injected when you read any .toml file.**
